### Tupay Ledger & Settlement Engine - API Test Suite
### REST Client tests for VS Code REST Client extension
### Use Ctrl+Alt+R to send requests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api
@contentType = application/json

### ============================================================================
### SECTION 1: AUTHENTICATION & 2FA
### ============================================================================

### 1.1: Login (get Sanctum bearer token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("bearer_token", response.body.token);
  client.global.set("user_id", response.body.user.id);
%}

### 1.2: Login with invalid password (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### ============================================================================
### SECTION 2: 2FA CHALLENGE - GET EAT TOKEN
### ============================================================================

### 2.1: Generate valid TOTP code (use the secret from database)
### NOTE: Must be run within 30 seconds of viewing the TOTP secret
### For test@example.com, get totp_secret from: select totp_secret from users where email='test@example.com'
### Then generate code using: php artisan tinker > TOTP::create($secret)->now()

### 2.2: Challenge with valid TOTP code (gets EAT token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/2fa/challenge
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "totp_code": "000000",
  "action_payload": {
    "source_currency": "NGN",
    "destination_currency": "CNY",
    "amount": 100000000
  }
}

> {%
  client.global.set("eat_token", response.body.eat_token);
%}

### 2.3: Challenge with invalid TOTP code (should fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/2fa/challenge
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "totp_code": "999999",
  "action_payload": {
    "source_currency": "NGN",
    "destination_currency": "CNY",
    "amount": 100000000
  }
}

### 2.4: Challenge without authentication (should fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/2fa/challenge
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "totp_code": "000000",
  "action_payload": {
    "source_currency": "NGN",
    "destination_currency": "CNY",
    "amount": 100000000
  }
}

### ============================================================================
### SECTION 3: SWAP EXECUTION
### ============================================================================

### 3.1: Swap with valid EAT token (should succeed with 200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/swap
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}
X-Elevated-Action-Token: {{eat_token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_currency": "NGN",
  "destination_currency": "CNY",
  "amount": 100000000
}

> {%
  if (response.status === 200) {
    client.global.set("transaction_id", response.body.transaction.id);
  }
%}

### 3.2: Swap without EAT token (should fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/swap
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_currency": "NGN",
  "destination_currency": "CNY",
  "amount": 100000000
}

### 3.3: Swap with invalid EAT token (should fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/swap
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}
X-Elevated-Action-Token: invalid-token-xyz
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_currency": "NGN",
  "destination_currency": "CNY",
  "amount": 100000000
}

### 3.4: Swap with expired EAT token (should fail - token has 60s TTL)
### Wait 61+ seconds, then try using the same EAT token again
POST {{baseUrl}}/swap
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}
X-Elevated-Action-Token: {{eat_token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_currency": "NGN",
  "destination_currency": "CNY",
  "amount": 100000000
}

### 3.5: Swap with insufficient balance (should fail with 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/swap
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}
X-Elevated-Action-Token: {{eat_token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_currency": "NGN",
  "destination_currency": "CNY",
  "amount": 9999999999999
}

### 3.6: Swap with self-currency (should fail - NGN to NGN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/swap
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}
X-Elevated-Action-Token: {{eat_token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_currency": "NGN",
  "destination_currency": "NGN",
  "amount": 100000000
}

### ============================================================================
### SECTION 4: LEDGER HISTORY
### ============================================================================

### 4.1: Get ledger entries for NGN wallet (with pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ledger/1?page=1&per_page=10
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}

### 4.2: Get ledger with page 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/ledger/1?page=2&per_page=10
Authorization: Bearer {{bearer_token}}

### ============================================================================
### SECTION 5: SETTLEMENT WEBHOOK
### ============================================================================

### 5.1: Settlement webhook with VALID signature
### Signature must be: HMAC-SHA256(json_encode(payload), SETTLEMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET)
### For test env, secret is typically 'test-secret-key'

POST {{baseUrl}}/webhook/settlement
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "transaction_id": 1,
  "status": "completed",
  "settled_at": "2026-08-05T12:00:00Z",
  "signature": "calculate-hmac-sha256-signature-here"
}

### 5.2: Settlement webhook with INVALID signature (should fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhook/settlement
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "transaction_id": 1,
  "status": "completed",
  "settled_at": "2026-08-05T12:00:00Z",
  "signature": "invalid-signature-xyz"
}

### 5.3: Settlement webhook for non-existent transaction (should fail with 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhook/settlement
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "transaction_id": 99999,
  "status": "completed",
  "settled_at": "2026-08-05T12:00:00Z",
  "signature": "valid-signature-here"
}

### 5.4: Settlement webhook marking as failed (status = failed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhook/settlement
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "transaction_id": 1,
  "status": "failed",
  "settled_at": "2026-08-05T12:00:00Z",
  "signature": "valid-signature-here"
}

### ============================================================================
### HELPER: Calculate HMAC-SHA256 Signature
### ============================================================================
###
### To calculate valid webhook signature in bash:
###
### SECRET="test-secret-key"
### PAYLOAD='{"transaction_id":1,"status":"completed","settled_at":"2026-08-05T12:00:00Z"}'
### SIGNATURE=$(echo -n "$PAYLOAD" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "$SECRET" | cut -d' ' -f2)
### echo $SIGNATURE
###
### Or in PHP (for Laravel Tinker):
###
### php artisan tinker
### $secret = config('settlement.webhook_secret');
### $payload = json_encode(['transaction_id' => 1, 'status' => 'completed', 'settled_at' => '2026-08-05T12:00:00Z'], JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES);
### $signature = hash_hmac('sha256', $payload, $secret);
### echo $signature;
###
### ============================================================================

### ============================================================================
### NOTES ON TEST USERS
### ============================================================================
###
### Seeders create 2 test users:
### 1. test@example.com / password123
###    - Initial balance: 5M NGN (500,000,000 kobo), 500k CNY (50,000,000 fen)
###    - Has valid TOTP secret (generated randomly)
###
### 2. user@example.com / password123
###    - Initial balance: 5M NGN (500,000,000 kobo), 500k CNY (50,000,000 fen)
###    - Has valid TOTP secret (generated randomly)
###
### To get TOTP secret for testing:
### mysql> SELECT email, totp_secret FROM users;
###
### To generate valid TOTP code:
### php artisan tinker
### $user = User::where('email', 'test@example.com')->first();
### $totp = TOTP::create($user->totp_secret);
### echo $totp->now();  // Valid for 30 seconds
###
### ============================================================================